{
  "$comment": [
    "Milestone 6 route walker and validator measurements (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §9.2-§9.4; §14 budgets walk + simulate + validate of a 10,000-step route at 20 ms or less). Re-measured after the Milestone 6 review fixes (2026-09-26, sim-engine-validate).",
    "Two routes, both from tests/bench/bench-support.ts (review PERF-01). realistic: the quests the sample character (Horde Orc warrior, fresh history) can take, ordered by level, written as a guide writes them and repaired with the validator (620 quests; 387 issues, 1 error), padded to 10,000 steps with 6,680 travel waypoints between consecutive located steps. The §14 budget applies to it; its padding is the cheapest kind of step, so it flatters as much as the stress route penalises (the owner decides the budget scope). stress: the earlier route (every quest with a single NPC starter and finisher and kill or item objectives, as accept, complete and turn-in, a hearth every 25th cycle and a grind every 40th, repeated; prerequisites ignored; 10,423 issues). It is a regression guard for scaling, with a ceiling of twice the budget (40 ms) on a warm walk + validate and on an edit.",
    "Stored baselines (route10000.<route>.<case>, validate10000.<route>.<case>): pnpm exec tsx tests/bench/engine.bench.ts --check docs/measurements/engine-m6.json --repeat 3 --runs 15, and the same for validate.bench.ts (review PERF-04). The script bundles itself with esbuild (no tsx keepNames wrapper, as a production build), runs each gated case in a fresh process 3 times in rotating order, 15 runs after 3 warm-ups per process, and times the CPU probe (2e7 square-root loop, median of 5) in the same process. medianMs is the median of the processes' medians; normalised = medianMs x 40 / probeMs (40 ms is this machine's calm probe, docs/measurements/map-m3.json). --check fails when a normalised median is more than 25% over the stored normalised median, or over its limit.",
    "Load: two stale background processes kept about two CPU cores busy throughout; the probe read 40.2-42.2 ms (the median of five runs, of which two took about 53 ms). Absolute numbers are noisy: compare within one table.",
    "reviewAB is the interleaved A/B of the review: the critic's harness (.cache/m6-critic/perf/harness.ts; cold = a fresh copy of the effective rules) bundled against three snapshots of src (before the fixes; with the correctness fixes; with the correctness and performance fixes), run in turn per case and route, 21 iterations after 3 warm-ups per process, 3 repetitions. Each cell is the median of the 3 process medians, with their min and max. walk-new and validate-new are a new walker (and validator) on the same rules and dataset (a context change that keeps both); publish-edit-end is an edit of the last step walked and its route metrics taken, as the app publishes it; metrics-full is aggregateRouteMetrics over the whole walk."
  ],
